@0    = ~The bed is freshly made and ready to use. At least, it would be, but you can't fold the bed down. The cat is in the way.~
@1    = ~A stray cat that has found a home in the monastery. The Ilmateri monks seem to take their mission of caring for the needy very seriously, indeed.~
@2    = ~The cat looks at you.~
@3    = ~You reach down to pet her.~
@4    = ~I want to fold down the bed. Would you step aside a bit, hmm?~
@5    = ~This dead rat is from you, yes? A present? That was *so* nice of you, Moggy. Thank you *so* much!~
@6    = ~Would you stop putting dead vermin into my chest?~
@7    = ~You leave the cat be.~
//@8
@9    = ~Moggy strokes around your legs, obviously very pleased with herself.~
@10   = ~Moggy lets you pet her.~
@11   = ~Moggy lets you pet her, but her tail is twitching.~
@12   = ~Moggy lost patience. You get a scratch from her claws.~
@13   = ~This was not the time! You sparked Moggy's wrath! The cat bites you.~
@14   = ~You earned Moggy's favor. The cat purrs, her eyes half closed. A moment of complete peace.~
@15   = ~The cat gives you a look, making it perfectly clear that she can sit wherever she wants for as long as she wants—but because she really, really feels generous today, she might consider stepping aside... in a minute.~
@16   = ~Moggy lost interest and walked away.~
